        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): guard act hooks on current tab URL",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`/hooks/file-chooser` and `/hooks/dialog` can trigger page-side effects, but they did not opt into the current-tab URL guard used by guarded `/act` routes. A request could arm uploads, click an upload control, or patch dialog functions while the selected tab was already on a disallowed URL.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe shared route helper already supports `enforceCurrentUrlAllowed`. File chooser and dialog hooks should use the same current-tab safety contract before running page-affecting hook code.\n\nThis branch also aligns the route test's `withBrowserNavigationPolicy` mock with the real helper by omitting the default `browserProxyMode: \"direct\"`; that keeps the focused regression test asserting the same shape production passes to the navigation guard.\n\n## User Impact\n\nFile chooser and dialog hooks now fail closed before page side effects when the current tab URL is blocked by browser navigation policy.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Enabled `enforceCurrentUrlAllowed` on both hook routes.\n- Added route-level regressions proving file chooser and dialog hooks return before upload/dialog side effects on a blocked current tab.\n- Focused tests/checks on head `7c93b2c6330db11c55eab2d9f717e83e4339692d`:\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/agent.act.hooks.current-url-guard.test.ts -- --reporter=verbose` (1 file, 2 tests)\n  - `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/agent.act.hooks.current-url-guard.test.ts`\n  - `OPENCLAW_OXLINT_SKIP_PREPARE=1 node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/agent.act.hooks.current-url-guard.test.ts`\n  - `git diff --check`\n  - `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --engine claude` clean, no accepted/actionable findings\n\n## Proof\n\nThe focused tests run locally with mocked Playwright and Chrome MCP side effects. They prove the guard fires before upload path resolution, upload/click actions, dialog patching, or Playwright dialog arming.\n\nA real Chrome/bridge proof was also run against the previous production-code head `8d500187dad1e0be24245217f0a25116029e4b8f` before the test-only mock alignment commit. It covered allowed and blocked file chooser and dialog flows:\n\n- allowed file chooser returned HTTP 200 `{ ok: true }`; page observed `uploadChangeCount=1` and `uploadFileName=proof-upload.txt`\n- blocked file chooser returned HTTP 400 `browser navigation blocked by policy`; page observed `uploadChangeCount=0`\n- allowed dialog hook returned HTTP 200 `{ ok: true }`; page observed `dialogResult=true`\n- blocked dialog hook returned HTTP 400 `browser navigation blocked by policy`; page observed `dialogResult=false` after manual CDP dismissal\n",
        "branch": "llagy007/browser-hooks-current-url-guard-20260711",
